---
name: "Simple Example"
markup: true
variables:
  name: ""
  greeting: ""
  date: ""
  time: ""
  line1: ""
  documentName: ""
  documentType: ""
  paragraphbody: ""
---
#SCRIPT
if system.time < "12:00":
    greeting = "Good morning"
elif system.time > "12:00" and  system.time < "18:00":
    greeting = "Good afternoon"
else:
    greeting = "Good evening"

date = system.date
time = system.time

match documentType:
    case "report":
        line1 = "this is a document"
    case "essay":
        line1 = "this is perhaps an essay"
    case _:
        line1 = "unknown document type"
   
#ENDSCRIPT
\section{Introduction To SimplyDraft}
{greeting} {name}! This example is a simple showcase of what SimplyDraft is capable of.

Today is {date}, and the time is {time}.

\subsection{Key Features}
\begin{itemize}
\item Text can be edited simply in the Content Pane
\item You can create variables by using curly brackets (no spaces inside the brackets!)
\item You can write Python scripting in the Script Pane to set the variable values
\item You can format the document using LaTeX-like markups
\item Click the ? buttons to learn more about the Python-like scripting & LaTeX-like markups
\end{itemize}

\subsection{QOL Features}
\begin{itemize}
\item You can set theme or accent changes in the menu header
\item There are keyboard shortcuts! Click on the menu headers to learn more
\item Files and logs are saved to \%LOCALAPPDATA\%SimplyDraft
\end{itemize}

\subsection{Examples!}
Title of Document: {documentName}
Type of Document: {documentType}
{line1}

\pagebreak
